CHAPTER.VERS:
We must have consideration of those who are appointed to the ministry of the word, and the government of the church of God, and who do their duty. And we beseech you, brethren, to
That you acknowledge and take them for such as they are, that is to say, men worthy to be greatly esteemed of among you. know them which labour among you, and are over you in the
In those things which pertain to God's service: so is the ecclesiastical function distinguished from civil authority, and true shepherds from wolves. Lord, and admonish you;
